{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1125481-what-would-your-character-do-w-tf-edition","id":1125481,"title":"What would your character do ? (W:TF edition)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-05T21:39:47-07:00","id":1125481,"title":"What would your character do ? (W:TF edition)","content":"I did something in the W:TA forums a couple days ago and I decided to do it here as well. The rules are simple, I give you a situation and you have to answer how your character would solve it.<br /> <br /> Here is the first scenario.<br /> \u200bYou are currently tracking prey that is a member of a mafia family. You managed to track him down to a funeral party that is mourning the loss of his father, the Don of the family. He is currently in the funeral home shortly after the burial discussing business with his brothers. The home is heavily guarded and the goombas that surround the home won't hesitate to shoot you if you do a direct assault. What do you do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T22:07:19-07:00","id":1125485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1125481-what-would-your-character-do-w-tf-edition#post1125481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did something in the W:TA forums a couple days ago and I decided to do it here as well. The rules are simple, I give you a situation and you have to answer how your character would solve it.<br /> <br /> Here is the first scenario.<br /> \u200bYou are currently tracking prey that is a member of a mafia family. You managed to track him down to a funeral party that is mourning the loss of his father, the Don of the family. He is currently in the funeral home shortly after the burial discussing business with his brothers. The home is heavily guarded and the goombas that surround the home won't hesitate to shoot you if you do a direct assault. What do you do?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Go get my mage friend to solve it via space magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T23:18:40-07:00","id":1125496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1125481-what-would-your-character-do-w-tf-edition#post1125481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did something in the W:TA forums a couple days ago and I decided to do it here as well. The rules are simple, I give you a situation and you have to answer how your character would solve it.<br /> <br /> Here is the first scenario.<br /> \u200bYou are currently tracking prey that is a member of a mafia family. You managed to track him down to a funeral party that is mourning the loss of his father, the Don of the family. He is currently in the funeral home shortly after the burial discussing business with his brothers. The home is heavily guarded and the goombas that surround the home won't hesitate to shoot you if you do a direct assault. What do you do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fun!<br /> <br /> My guy hasn't been played in a while but I'll use him. Realistically, he might sneak his way in, then attempt to get the target alone and kill them, then make a hasty escape. But he does try to be cunning, and he's got the Renown to show for it. His plans often go bad, but gauru is more than enough to kill a few gunmen and a room full of gangsters. Still, try to be sneakier first.<br /> <br /> So. Luna's Embrace and a nice black outfit to fit in with the mourning crowd. Manage to get into one-on-one conversation with target. Lay the Hunter's Aspect on him, then Gaze of the Moon with a Delusion whammy so he runs away. Once he's outside, Command Artifice and order a car to run him over.<br /> <br /> My character had to do something like this at a hospital once, but I think he managed to just sneak in, get the job done, then sneak out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T08:12:12-07:00","id":1125601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1125481-what-would-your-character-do-w-tf-edition#post1125481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is the first scenario.<br /> \u200bYou are currently tracking prey that is a member of a mafia family. You managed to track him down to a funeral party that is mourning the loss of his father, the Don of the family. He is currently in the funeral home shortly after the burial discussing business with his brothers. The home is heavily guarded and the goombas that surround the home won't hesitate to shoot you if you do a direct assault. What do you do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming the objective is to kill the target, I'd get a Talen with the Catastrophe facet and drown the funerary home in flames from the shadow, while most of the high ranking members of the organization are inside for a bonus, and without evidence of my presence to earn retaliation. Yes, yes, my pack's name should be something akin to &quot;Those who answer dispropotionately&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T09:56:15-07:00","id":1125618,"title":"","content":"Ok, here is a second scenario <br /> \u200bFor months, you have been tracking a new prey, the head of some kind of self-help cult who some type of connection to the Azlu. As you are about to corner this prey, you are suddenly knocked out with a shovel. When you wake up, you find out you have been buried alive in a coffin. What does your character do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T10:25:19-07:00","id":1125629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1125481-what-would-your-character-do-w-tf-edition?p=1125618#post1125618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, here is a second scenario<br /> \u200bFor months, you have been tracking a new prey, the head of some kind of self-help cult who some type of connection to the Azlu. As you are about to corner this prey, you are suddenly knocked out with a shovel. When you wake up, you find out you have been buried alive in a coffin. What does your character do?</div> </div> </div> </div>You know it's pretty damned difficult to knock out an Uratha, right?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T10:27:04-07:00","id":1125632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1125481-what-would-your-character-do-w-tf-edition?p=1125629#post1125629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know it's pretty damned difficult to knock out an Uratha, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, I will just scrap that Scenario then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T10:33:39-07:00","id":1125635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1125481-what-would-your-character-do-w-tf-edition?p=1125618#post1125618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, here is a second scenario<br /> \u200bFor months, you have been tracking a new prey, the head of some kind of self-help cult who some type of connection to the Azlu. As you are about to corner this prey, you are suddenly knocked out with a shovel. When you wake up, you find out you have been buried alive in a coffin. What does your character do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of an easy one. Moldywarp. 'This Facet can only be used while in Dalu. The Uratha\u2019s hands transform into broad, powerful claws that can tunnel through solid materials at a steady pace. She easily tears aside earth, rock, and concrete. The Uratha gains a tunneling Speed equal to her Strength + Cunning Renown.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T13:20:09-07:00","id":1125674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1125481-what-would-your-character-do-w-tf-edition?p=1125635#post1125635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">'Moldywarp.This Facet can only be used while in Dalu. '</div> </div> </div> </div><i><b>Gift for rework detected</b></i>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T13:39:20-07:00","id":1125682,"title":"","content":"Here is a other scenario<br /> It is Christmas Eve. Your prey has fled into a crowded shopping center. You end up losing your prey in the crowd of thousands of holiday shoppers. What does your character do to track it down without letting the Herd know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T13:50:14-07:00","id":1125684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Story Letter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1125481-what-would-your-character-do-w-tf-edition?p=1125674#post1125674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><b>Gift for rework detected</b></i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can just get a fetish to let you use it in different circumstances. Fetishes can alter the effects of Facets.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12186\" data-vbnamecard=\"12186\">Killerclown</a> Thinking about this one. Obviously if you've tasted their blood you can just zero in on them so presumably we're going without that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T14:15:00-07:00","id":1125688,"title":"","content":"To the first scenario, it would depend on whether or not we were doing first edition or second edition. I've only done one werewolf character, so I'm likely to base the actions on what she'd do. Which in this case would be to infiltrate it using parkour then utilize the gift of scherezade's to cause people to sit and listen to her sing. While she was doing that, my packmates would take a more direct path, with the Warrior in our group dealing with anyone who gathers the sense to resist and getting their attention... and our irraka does what irraka do. If this were second edition, it'd be a little different because that gift isn't around anymore. Is this at night or day? If it's night, we have the advantage of vision and mobility. Parkour so that I don't have to take a direct path, find a way to the electric box, cut off the sources of their light. My entire pack then channels their inner Batman.<br /> <br /> Which, now that I think of it, should always be the answer. So change my first edition answer.<br /> <br /> In regards to being stuck in the coffin, I would lack the moldywarp facet unfortunately. Fortunately my pack has multiple pack related gifts, and I'd probably utilize them to alert the pack that something weird was going on with me. It's quite embarassing as a Storm Lord to require your pack to dig you out, but sometimes you have to have faith in the people around you to get you out of a situation you can't yourself. #Family<br /> <br /> For the third scenario... I myself think I'd need to know more about my prey to figure out the exact method I'd use. Are they aware I am hunting them? I'm assuming in this scenario that I have not tasted their blood or done anything that would seem basic for tracking..? I can't help but feel like I would lean on my Ithaeur for this one since she spends so much of her time shopping... she probably knows the center like the back of her hand and has all sorts of spirit friends there... :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T14:39:36-07:00","id":1125693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1125481-what-would-your-character-do-w-tf-edition?p=1125684#post1125684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can just get a fetish to let you use it in different circumstances. Fetishes can alter the effects of Facets.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think I will stick to the rework and add the fetish later on <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> Like that they work in all form but they give initiative penalty while using them. Or maybe that they work only in forms with hands and claws, partial transformation may make this gift possible to use in other forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12906-story-letter","name":"Story Letter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12906_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T15:28:38-07:00","id":1125708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1125481-what-would-your-character-do-w-tf-edition?p=1125682#post1125682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is Christmas Eve. Your prey has fled into a crowded shopping center. You end up losing your prey in the crowd of thousands of holiday shoppers. What does your character do to track it down without letting the Herd know?</div> </div> </div> </div>Might have to call in the pack for this, but that's what Hishu's for. Even if I can't use the pack my character does have good perception, and can shift into a different form in someplace private for better perception. Then we activate <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-giver-of-gifts-2-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\">City Eyes</a> to flip around until I spot him and go after him from there. Thank you, Giver of Gifts, I had been using it four all our surveillance stuff, though I didn't have it in the hospital I did have it when we were going after the vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T16:09:59-07:00","id":1125725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1125481-what-would-your-character-do-w-tf-edition?p=1125682#post1125682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is a other scenario<br /> It is Christmas Eve. Your prey has fled into a crowded shopping center. You end up losing your prey in the crowd of thousands of holiday shoppers. What does your character do to track it down without letting the Herd know?</div> </div> </div> </div>Track the prey with Impossible Spoor, follow it till it's on a more suitable spot such as near it's Safe Place and take it down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T17:42:08-07:00","id":1125739,"title":"","content":"Yeah just a tracking roll would really be good for that. Throw in Honed Senses and Impossible Spoor and no one's getting away without some help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T11:54:20-07:00","id":1125977,"title":"","content":"<b> Scenario Four</b> <br /> You've tracked your Host target to a prestigious reception. It has called its kind to attack the party and cause chaos and/or take over as many of the guests as possible. They will arrive in 1 hour. A violent incident will likely lead to a lock-down. How do you locate your Target and eliminate them without the Herd noticing? Then remove the threat of the remaining Hosts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T12:25:27-07:00","id":1125988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1125481-what-would-your-character-do-w-tf-edition?p=1125977#post1125977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b> Scenario Four</b><br /> You've tracked your Host target to a prestigious reception. It has called its kind to attack the party and cause chaos and/or take over as many of the guests as possible. They will arrive in 1 hour. A violent incident will likely lead to a lock-down. How do you locate your Target and eliminate them without the Herd noticing? Then remove the threat of the remaining Hosts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Lore of the Land and senses to find the target.<br /> <br /> Then just kill them. If I can do it in private, that's good, but my guy's only good with combat in gauru or urshul. I can Command Artifice to let any doors to let me out.<br /> <br /> If every witness is going to be dead in an hour it won't matter if they know or not. So I'll be sure to get out of there before the rest of the Hosts come.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T12:56:17-07:00","id":1126003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1125481-what-would-your-character-do-w-tf-edition?p=1125988#post1125988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lore of the Land and senses to find the target.<br /> <br /> Then just kill them. If I can do it in private, that's good, but my guy's only good with combat in gauru or urshul. I can Command Artifice to let any doors to let me out.<br /> <br /> If every witness is going to be dead in an hour it won't matter if they know or not. So I'll be sure to get out of there before the rest of the Hosts come.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, better they die human than become mockeries of the natural order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T13:07:52-07:00","id":1126008,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1125481-what-would-your-character-do-w-tf-edition?p=1125988#post1125988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lore of the Land and senses to find the target.<br /> <br /> Then just kill them. If I can do it in private, that's good, but my guy's only good with combat in gauru or urshul. I can Command Artifice to let any doors to let me out.<br /> <br /> If every witness is going to be dead in an hour it won't matter if they know or not. So I'll be sure to get out of there before the rest of the Hosts come.</div> </div> </div> </div>Problem is people are going to notice, and there is at least some media attention. You could command any cameras to stop working and slaughter everyone, I suppose. That's still going to cause an investigation, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-07-2017, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T13:17:04-07:00","id":1126013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1125481-what-would-your-character-do-w-tf-edition?p=1126008#post1126008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Problem is people are going to notice, and there is at least some media attention. You could command any cameras to stop working and slaughter everyone, I suppose. That's still going to cause an investigation, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>The host called for reinforcements, right? They're going to get there and kill or take over people. That's not my character's concern. He's after one Host. The urban fantasy superhero thing was first edition. In second edition, the Wolf Must Hunt.<br /> <br /> If there's cameras, then yes I would avoid turning into a giant wolf in front of them. But since the other humans will be dead after the reinforcements come, the hosts are keeping the oath for me.<br /> <br /> I'm sure there would be an investigation, but they're going to find monster spiders or giant rat swarms, not evidence of werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-07-2017, 04:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T13:30:29-07:00","id":1126022,"title":"","content":"Nuke-em from orbit. It's the only way to be sure.<br /> <br /> In all seriousness though, what kind of Host is this? They sort of... propagate differently, last I checked. I mean if the option is letting them become hosts or letting them die as humans, I'd probably commit a rather mundane action of setting the location on fire. But depending on what manner of beast we're dealing with, there might be other options to resort to. I'm assuming 'spider'.<br /> <br /> Actually... killing all the humans doesn't stop the fact that there are shard pieces of some spirit god looking for bodies does it..? This knowledge might be a blessing in disguise. Wait an hour for them to start taking the bodies of the victims, then burn the place down with them in it. Most likely, a host is not going to have cameras witnessing it and its kind taking over all these people, so I'm not particularly worried about that (and if they are, they are likely local cameras, not off site). Welcome to MY parlor, said the wolf to the spider.<br /> <br /> Media attention is the lesser of two evils, here. Especially if you can make that media attention directed at the burning of a house with people in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1513-jakondite","name":"Jakondite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T15:11:13-07:00","id":1126070,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1125481-what-would-your-character-do-w-tf-edition?p=1126013#post1126013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The host called for reinforcements, right? They're going to get there and kill or take over people. That's not my character's concern. He's after one Host. The urban fantasy superhero thing was first edition. In second edition, the Wolf Must Hunt.<br /> <br /> If there's cameras, then yes I would avoid turning into a giant wolf in front of them. But since the other humans will be dead after the reinforcements come, the hosts are keeping the oath for me.<br /> <br /> I'm sure there would be an investigation, but they're going to find monster spiders or giant rat swarms, not evidence of werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.<br /> <br /> Especially if you follow it up with Jakondite's suggestion and burn down the place once the Hosts get inside.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T16:54:54-07:00","id":1126107,"title":"","content":"I don't have the Elemental Gifts, unfortunately, otherwise things would be a lot easier, and messier. I've loved the Elemental Gifts, and Weather Gifts, but they just didn't fit my character, who is totally a cityslicker. I could use Command Artifice to crash a plane into the building but that seems like overkill for one guy. I wanted to save it for the vampires in his game, though.<br /> <br /> If it's my character, it's likely not his territory, so in the end the hosts would be someone else's problem to deal with. One thing's for sure, he wouldn't linger around to pick a fight with a swarm of oncoming shartha. In-and-out is a much better plan for him. Better to be long gone before they ever arrive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-07-2017, 07:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T17:06:30-07:00","id":1126109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1125481-what-would-your-character-do-w-tf-edition?p=1126107#post1126107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have the Elemental Gifts, unfortunately, otherwise things would be a lot easier, and messier. I've loved the Elemental Gifts, and Weather Gifts, but they just didn't fit my character, who is totally a cityslicker. I could use Command Artifice to crash a plane into the building but that seems like overkill for one guy. I wanted to save it for the vampires in his game, though.<br /> <br /> If it's my character, it's likely not his territory, so in the end the hosts would be someone else's problem to deal with. One thing's for sure, he wouldn't linger around to pick a fight with a swarm of oncoming shartha. In-and-out is a much better plan for him. Better to be long gone before they ever arrive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, even without the Gift of the Elements, accelerants are a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T17:35:45-07:00","id":1126116,"title":"","content":"Here is scenario the 5th.<br /> <br /> You are tearing up a laboratory belonging to a tech firm that worshipps a Idigam still stranded on the moon. As you look for the scientists, the door, which is reinforced with steel, suddenly closes and locks on it's own. Then poison gas starts to fill the room . How do you get out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T18:45:57-07:00","id":1126136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1125481-what-would-your-character-do-w-tf-edition?p=1126116#post1126116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is scenario the 5th.<br /> <br /> You are tearing up a laboratory belonging to a tech firm that worshipps a Idigam still stranded on the moon. As you look for the scientists, the door, which is reinforced with steel, suddenly closes and locks on it's own. Then poison gas starts to fill the room . How do you get out?</div> </div> </div> </div>Command Artifice, tell the door to open and the mechanism with the gas to turn off. This is one of those things there's a lot of powers for. All Doors Open, Unmake, Entropy's Toll, you could use Sculpt and just fold the gas jets closed and make a hole in the door. And there's always the good old fashioned beat your way through the door. A writer beat up a tank with a rahu during playtesting.<br /> <br /> Same situation actually happened to my changeling, though it wasn't an idigam or scientists, he got trapped behind a remote controlled door and gassed to unconsciousness. I think he got out by shifting to Twilight and just running out of the building.<br /> <br /> I like this thread but surely some other werewolf players have characters who'd go about things differently?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-07-2017, 09:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T19:04:55-07:00","id":1126142,"title":"","content":"Good strategy. I am wondering if a Urathra would waste time looking for the scientists?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T19:28:11-07:00","id":1126143,"title":"","content":"Oh definitely, especially if they're worshiping something strange from space. My character would probably take a few hard drives and scientist pieces home to use Bone Gnaw with to uncover their secrets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-07T20:31:23-07:00","id":1126152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1125481-what-would-your-character-do-w-tf-edition?p=1125977#post1125977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b> Scenario Four</b> <br /> You've tracked your Host target to a prestigious reception. It has called its kind to attack the party and cause chaos and/or take over as many of the guests as possible. They will arrive in 1 hour. A violent incident will likely lead to a lock-down. How do you locate your Target and eliminate them without the Herd noticing? Then remove the threat of the remaining Hosts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Set the fire alarm going, wait till people evacuate. Keep tracking the specific host till you get it. If more hosts swarm a place with authorities that's really on them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1125481-what-would-your-character-do-w-tf-edition?p=1126116#post1126116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is scenario the 5th.<br /> <br /> You are tearing up a laboratory belonging to a tech firm that worshipps a Idigam still stranded on the moon. As you look for the scientists, the door, which is reinforced with steel, suddenly closes and locks on it's own. Then poison gas starts to fill the room. How do you get out?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got a brand fetish that allows me to order the spirits of things around by modifying Spirit Whispers, can order the gas mechanism to stop and/or open the doors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 08-07-2017, 11:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T13:51:18-07:00","id":1126832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1125481-what-would-your-character-do-w-tf-edition#post1125481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is the first scenario.<br /> \u200bYou are currently tracking prey that is a member of a mafia family. You managed to track him down to a funeral party that is mourning the loss of his father, the Don of the family. He is currently in the funeral home shortly after the burial discussing business with his brothers. The home is heavily guarded and the goombas that surround the home won't hesitate to shoot you if you do a direct assault. What do you do?</div> </div> </div> </div>We'd of course have spent time constructing a Plan (CofD pg100). Based on what my Prophetic Dreams revealed about this part of the Siskur-Dah, the night before a ghost at the funeral home is going to have a hard time not being persuaded to push the Mafia tough guy down the stairs especially when we offer something it asks for. Fortunately, our Pack has Residential Area from our Totem and we call in a favors get access to an ambulance and some EMT uniforms, our Irraka would help convince them he needed the ride, and even if enforcers rode with us it'd be short work once we pull into somewhere we can push them out, do the slaughter, and then hose down the pavement without witnesses. Doesn't even matter if they attempt to follow use because their cars will betray them due to the Rahu's help.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1125481-what-would-your-character-do-w-tf-edition?p=1125682#post1125682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is a other scenario<br /> It is Christmas Eve. Your prey has fled into a crowded shopping center. You end up losing your prey in the crowd of thousands of holiday shoppers. What does your character do to track it down without letting the Herd know?</div> </div> </div> </div>Make a quick Plan (CofD pg100) about covering the exits, organizing who goes where to optimize our chance of catching them leave, and wait. My Prophetic Dreams revealed to me it'd be difficult for the prey to escape our notice while leaving. If the prey isn't caught by us leaving and isn't a mere human I'd use Lore of the Land after the shopping center closes to see if it's still inside, if it is... ho-ho-ho time for a Very Merry Sacred Hunt, if you know what I mean. If we do catch it leaving then we trail it. If it is neither there nor did we catch it leaving then the Ithaeur uses Impossible Spore to pick up the trail.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1125481-what-would-your-character-do-w-tf-edition?p=1125977#post1125977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b> Scenario Four</b><br /> You've tracked your Host target to a prestigious reception. It has called its kind to attack the party and cause chaos and/or take over as many of the guests as possible. They will arrive in 1 hour. A violent incident will likely lead to a lock-down. How do you locate your Target and eliminate them without the Herd noticing? Then remove the threat of the remaining Hosts?</div> </div> </div> </div>Host's collecting in one spot? We can cause a lock down after they enter?! Sounds amazing!! Obviously after the lock down my Elidoth Packmate would Shutdown and All Doors Lock that place so hard. Not much for my character to do except to help carry the gas cans and turn into a slaughter machine when the killing time come. <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/FateWorseThanDeath\" target=\"_blank\">Many humans will die, but it's better than allowing them to become Hosts</a>. Of course the building is getting burned down when we're done. Uratha are good People, but not good people. By the way, did I mention we'd have a Plan (CofD pg100)?<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jakondite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1125481-what-would-your-character-do-w-tf-edition?p=1126022#post1126022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This knowledge might be a blessing in disguise. Wait an hour for them to start taking the bodies of the victims, then burn the place down with them in it. Most likely, a host is not going to have cameras witnessing it and its kind taking over all these people, so I'm not particularly worried about that (and if they are, they are likely local cameras, not off site). Welcome to MY parlor, said the wolf to the spider.<br /> <br /> Media attention is the lesser of two evils, here. Especially if you can make that media attention directed at the burning of a house with people in it.</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> Basically what they said^<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Killerclown</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1125481-what-would-your-character-do-w-tf-edition?p=1126116#post1126116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is scenario the 5th.<br /> <br /> You are tearing up a laboratory belonging to a tech firm that worships a Idigam still stranded on the moon. As you look for the scientists, the door, which is reinforced with steel, suddenly closes and locks on it's own. Then poison gas starts to fill the room . How do you get out?</div> </div> </div> </div>If only I could assume a form capable of rending steel... wait, I have Living Weapon 5 so I can!! Problem solved.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 08-09-2017, 07:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T14:17:53-07:00","id":1126846,"title":"","content":"Okay here's one from me.<br /> <br /> Wolf-blooded closest to your character has become overly enamored with a vampire. If you know about such things, you recognize it as a blood bond, but otherwise it's a sort of fawning obsession. Said vampire has come to you with an offer. Kill a powerful and well-protected elder in a nearby domain, outside of your territory, and she will erase the wolf-blooded's memory of her and leave town, never to be seen again. In the meantime, if she goes missing or gets killed by an angry werewolf, wolf-blooded will be shown evidence to suggest that the werewolf killed the vampire. Any attempts to detect deceit seem to suggest she's being honest with the deal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T15:53:17-07:00","id":1126864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1125481-what-would-your-character-do-w-tf-edition?p=1126846#post1126846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay here's one from me.<br /> <br /> Wolf-blooded closest to your character has become overly enamored with a vampire. If you know about such things, you recognize it as a blood bond, but otherwise it's a sort of fawning obsession. Said vampire has come to you with an offer. Kill a powerful and well-protected elder in a nearby domain, outside of your territory, and she will erase the wolf-blooded's memory of her and leave town, never to be seen again. In the meantime, if she goes missing or gets killed by an angry werewolf, wolf-blooded will be shown evidence to suggest that the werewolf killed the vampire. Any attempts to detect deceit seem to suggest she's being honest with the deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>First reach out to Vampire or Mage contacts and see if they are willing to trade a less BS task for a mind-wipe. Then stake the Leech and mail her to the elder with a note about what she was planning. When the evidence gets shown to the Wolf-Blood, they'll wonder who was that and why should they care? They've already had their memories of the vampire removed.<br /> <br /> She should have never tipped her hand like that. Examples have to get made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T16:49:15-07:00","id":1126887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1125481-what-would-your-character-do-w-tf-edition?p=1126846#post1126846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay here's one from me.<br /> <br /> Wolf-blooded closest to your character has become overly enamored with a vampire. If you know about such things, you recognize it as a blood bond, but otherwise it's a sort of fawning obsession. Said vampire has come to you with an offer. Kill a powerful and well-protected elder in a nearby domain, outside of your territory, and she will erase the wolf-blooded's memory of her and leave town, never to be seen again. In the meantime, if she goes missing or gets killed by an angry werewolf, wolf-blooded will be shown evidence to suggest that the werewolf killed the vampire. Any attempts to detect deceit seem to suggest she's being honest with the deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow... just wow. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1125481-what-would-your-character-do-w-tf-edition?p=1126846#post1126846\">Here's my answer to </a><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> It's like you know my character concept. Kevin McBride, aka Hissu-Ses a Bone Shadow Cahalith, is my character and his sister was drained to death by a vampire before Kevin's first change and stalking that vampire was what prompted his First Change. Lore of the Land and Barghest were his first two Shadow Gifts. Our Pack Ban is &quot;Never Deliberately help a Vampire&quot;. (Our Totem is my character's sister's ghost that has Essence Thief for Spirit Essence, the ST made an exception and I was the one that was willing to pay the 5 Totem points at character creation) So no deal, and the vampire is about die in ways that fulfill our Totem Aspiration as well... And we'll have to preemptively confess to the wolfblooded of what the vampire was trying to black mail us with, which is her death and earnestly seek to mend the relationship damage.<br /> <br /> It's like that plot was made for our pack.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Scenario from me:<br /> <br /> You just figured out all the female members of your pack are pregnant, <u><i>ALL </i>of them</u>, Uratha, Wolfblooded, and even the mortals, including those that don't engage in reproductive congress, use protection or otherwise wouldn't expect that from.<br /> <br /> Maybe a powerful spirit of fertility used Mass Create on them, but how would it do so without being noticed, which spirit did it, why would a spirit want more Uratha, and how are you going to handle the consequences? <br /> <br /> Most frighteningly, what if the issue was caused by something other than a spirit?<br /> <br /> For bonus points, this event has alerted every Cahalith within 100 miles through their Prophetic Dreams, and it seems that any of the resulting babies would be destined to undergo the First Change if they survived to maturity...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 08-09-2017, 08:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T19:52:44-07:00","id":1126939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1125481-what-would-your-character-do-w-tf-edition?p=1126864#post1126864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First reach out to Vampire or Mage contacts and see if they are willing to trade a less BS task for a mind-wipe. Then stake the Leech and mail her to the elder with a note about what she was planning. When the evidence gets shown to the Wolf-Blood, they'll wonder who was that and why should they care? They've already had their memories of the vampire removed.<br /> <br /> She should have never tipped her hand like that. Examples have to get made.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd make some fetish or rite for the purpose of the mind-wipe. Cut down the middle guy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T19:56:25-07:00","id":1126940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1125481-what-would-your-character-do-w-tf-edition?p=1126887#post1126887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wow... just wow. <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1125481-what-would-your-character-do-w-tf-edition?p=1126846#post1126846&amp;quot;]Here's</a> my answer to [/URL]<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> It's like you know my character concept. Kevin McBride, aka Hissu-Ses a Bone Shadow Cahalith, is my character and his sister was drained to death by a vampire before Kevin's first change and stalking that vampire was what prompted his First Change. Lore of the Land and Barghest were his first two Shadow Gifts. Our Pack Ban is &amp;quot;Never Deliberately help a Vampire&amp;quot;. (Our Totem is my character's sister's ghost that has Essence Thief for Spirit Essence, the ST made an exception and I was the one that was willing to pay the 5 Totem points at character creation) So no deal, and the vampire is about die in ways that fulfill our Totem Aspiration as well... And we'll have to preemptively confess to the wolfblooded of what the vampire was trying to black mail us with, which is her death and earnestly seek to mend the relationship damage.<br /> <br /> It's like that plot was made for our pack.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> Scenario from me:<br /> <br /> You just figured out all the female members of your pack are pregnant, <u><i>ALL </i>of them</u>, Uratha, Wolfblooded, and even the mortals, including those that don't engage in reproductive congress, use protection or otherwise wouldn't expect that from.<br /> <br /> Maybe a powerful spirit of fertility used Mass Create on them, but how would it do so without being noticed, which spirit did it, why would a spirit want more Uratha, and how are you going to handle the consequences? <br /> <br /> Most frighteningly, what if the issue was caused by something other than a spirit?<br /> <br /> For bonus points, this event has alerted every Cahalith within 100 miles through their Prophetic Dreams, and it seems that any of the resulting babies would be destined to undergo the First Change if they survived to maturity...</div> </div> </div> </div>Just try to figure what the fuck happened and open an abortion clinic for the underage 21 century virgin maries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-09T21:54:59-07:00","id":1126965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1125481-what-would-your-character-do-w-tf-edition?p=1126887#post1126887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow.. just wow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice coincidence!<br /> <br /> My character went through with it, though he had a closer relationship with the vampire than the wolf-blooded at that point, and no mage or other vampire contacts. He still has the elder's hands on his inventory list.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You just figured out all the female members of your pack are pregnant, <u><i>ALL </i>of them</u>, Uratha, Wolfblooded, and even the mortals, including those that don't engage in reproductive congress, use protection or otherwise wouldn't expect that from.<br /> <br /> Maybe a powerful spirit of fertility used Mass Create on them, but how would it do so without being noticed, which spirit did it, why would a spirit want more Uratha, and how are you going to handle the consequences?<br /> <br /> Most frighteningly, what if the issue was caused by something other than a spirit?<br /> <br /> For bonus points, this event has alerted every Cahalith within 100 miles through their Prophetic Dreams, and it seems that any of the resulting babies would be destined to undergo the First Change if they survived to maturity... </div> </div> </div>While not made for my character, one of the few spirits my character has a good relationship with is a fairly powerful fertility spirit, who would at least be able to answer some questions about the mystery. He'd be pretty angry, though, and the perpetrator would probably find themselves on the end of a sacred hunt, as one of the wolf-blooded in the pack likely to be afflicted is his girlfriend. Depending on the source and the opinions of those involved we'd try to get rid of the problem or find some painless way to see it through to birth. I certainly wouldn't trust the Cahalith to not interfere, but if they're willing to play ball it would be nice to have them to help play defense or potentially hand the babies off to.<br /> <br /> I'd expect the Pure to get wind of it, too, so I'd certainly be on guard from that front, as well as getting the territory into ultra defense mode.<br /> <br /> Also seriously hoping occasional use of Luna's Embrace hasn't made my character one of the susceptible ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T07:04:30-07:00","id":1127095,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar886_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"886\" data-vbnamecard=\"886\">nofather</a> I'd totally make you reprise Arnold's pregnancy role.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}